1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
How do you know your organization is using AI well?

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
When teams are more freed than constrained by what they build.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Too often, software ties its creators down.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Yesterday’s output blocks today’s higher-value work.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,200
TPS is the Toyota Production System.

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:27,000
Jidoka is one of its two pillars.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,500
Jidoka: automation with a human touch.

8
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,500
A broken thread stops the loom.

9
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,000
Human wisdom lives in the mechanism.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Instead of watching the loom—or CI…

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Let the stop call you.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Solve the problem. Preserve the judgment.

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Build known rules into simple checks that stop the work.

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Leave clear evidence for the next person—or AI.

15
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,800
Keep as little as possible.

16
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:11,500
The best part is no part.

17
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,000
Remove unnecessary parts. Preserve needed behavior.

18
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Build knowledge into the product.

19
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Free yourself for the next problem that matters.
